WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.500
TechNeeds IGDTUW is a student-run tech mentorship program.

00:04.500 --> 00:09.000
You learn by doing short missions, with a mentor beside you.

00:09.000 --> 00:14.600
Step 1: find a cohort. Pick a track like Web Dev, DSA, App Dev or ML. Beginner tracks need no experience.

00:14.600 --> 00:21.000
Step 2: register when it opens. Cohort launches are posted on the Events page with a sign-up link.

00:21.000 --> 00:25.200
Step 3: once you're selected, your mentor emails your enrollment number and a temporary password.

00:25.200 --> 00:31.000
Log in as a mentee with that number, then set your own password.

00:31.000 --> 00:39.000
Step 4: finish missions (videos, quizzes and projects) to earn points and keep your streak. Late videos and projects lose 1 point per day.

00:39.000 --> 00:45.000
Your AI card sums up your progress. Every highlighted fact comes from your real activity, and it stays private until you share it.

00:45.000 --> 00:54.500
Where it leads: real projects on your GitHub, hackathons like InnoVortex, the Techboard hall of fame, and becoming a mentor next year.

00:54.500 --> 01:00.000
Ready to join? Tap "I'm new: show me how" on the TechNeeds site.
